// Tracked wrapper so a clean checkout (no fleet credentials) still generates and builds.
//
// CloudPushSecrets.xcconfig is gitignored and user-created (template:
// CloudPushSecrets.example.xcconfig). It carries the FRWHOOP fleet push defaults baked into the
// app at build time:
//   NOOP_PUSH_ENDPOINT      — the Supabase Edge Function base (…/functions/v1/push)
//   NOOP_PUSH_TOKEN           — the fleet ingest token (opaque `noop_…`, NOT a JWT, NOT a B2 key)
//   NOOP_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY    — Supabase anon key for authenticated score reads (JWT session only)
// When the file is absent the $(NOOP_PUSH_*) Info.plist keys resolve to empty strings and the
// build simply has no export destination: cloud push stays off and cannot be enabled.
//
// The token is an ingest credential, not a session: it can only write batches/objects for the
// research user, and it is extractable from the app bundle by anyone with the binary. That is an
// accepted property of the consented-research-fleet model — do not put any other secret here.
NOOP_PUSH_ENDPOINT =
NOOP_PUSH_TOKEN =
NOOP_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY =
#include? "CloudPushSecrets.xcconfig"
